content:
A **Specimen** is anything a crew brings back through a [[gates|Gate]]: plants, water, stone, soil, shells, bone, residue, machinery, fragments of built things. Under the [[gate-evaluation-doctrine|Gate Evaluation Doctrine]], all of it is treated as a Specimen until it's properly evaluated, however obvious it seems.

> **At the Specimen intake counter, the morning after a return**
>
> "It's Redbark. Everyone knows it's Redbark."
>
> "Everyone knows *Redbark* is Redbark." The clerk tied the tag to the jar. "This is a piece of bark you say came off a Redbark tree. When the laboratory agrees, it can be Redbark too. Next."

After analysis, a Specimen is filed as one of:

- **Discarded Material**: nothing useful or anomalous found;
- **Research Specimen**: scientifically interesting, not yet useful;
- **Artifact**: a made object, or something like one, that needs its own study;
- **Resource Candidate**: evidence of an exploitable anomalous property;
- **Confirmed Resource**: at least one Function identified, and entered in the [Resource catalogue](discoveries.html#resources).

None of the first four is final. Something every new Expeditioner collects and every laboratory ignores can turn out, after the right research, to matter a great deal. The [Research](game.html#post-research) rule covers how hidden properties come to light.
